{
  "_README": [
    "Spec 067 S2 — the curated tool catalog (使用頻度の高いツール). Generated, never hand-edited:",
    "  .venv/bin/python tools/dify_base/marketplace.py catalog <org>/<name>/<version> … > templates/tool-catalog.json",
    "",
    "IDENTIFIERS: every dependency_identifier is the PUBLIC marketplace package checksum, keyed to",
    "(plugin, version) — the same in every workspace, resolvable with no login and no install. Verified",
    "byte-for-byte against this repo own workspace exports (projects/_drafts/3_3/workflows/main.yml:12,15).",
    "VERSIONS ARE PINNED because the hash is version-keyed. Re-run the generator to bump.",
    "",
    "NODE SHAPE — two counter-intuitive rules, both from docs/runtime-supplement.md (verified against a",
    "lint-clean build) and confirmed in vendor/dify-src:",
    "  * provider_type is \"builtin\", NOT \"plugin\" — tool_manager.py:985-987 dispatches BUILT_IN to the",
    "    PluginToolProviderController; all 16 real tool nodes in corpus/ use builtin.",
    "  * provider_name is the FULL 3-segment path, identical to provider_id (\"provider name doubled\").",
    "    A 2-segment value raises ValueError in provider_ids.py GenericProviderID.",
    "plugin_id (org/plugin) is the dependency-identifier prefix — the key tying a tool node to its",
    "dependencies entry (lint_plugin_hashes.py coverage gate).",
    "",
    "A plugin listed here is BUILDABLE even if nobody has installed it: Dify accepts the import and",
    "raises its own install prompt — but ONLY if the DSL carries a non-empty top-level dependencies",
    "array (the graph-derived fallback is dead above DSL 0.1.5). So: emit the tool node AND the",
    "dependencies entry. Never drop a tool node because the workspace lacks the plugin."
